\pard\pardeftab720\sl280\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Opus:\
The political alliances ARE adultery because ancient Near Eastern treaties were sealed with religious oaths invoking the gods of both parties. To enter a vassal treaty with Assyria or Egypt required acknowledging their gods as witnesses and guarantors, often installing their cult objects in your temples.\
When Ahaz became Assyria's vassal, 2 Kings 16:10-18 records him copying a Damascus altar, restructuring the temple, and removing temple furniture "because of the king of Assyria." The political submission required religious accommodation. This is literally taking another divine "husband" while married to YHWH.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl280\partightenfactor0
\cf2 <notes> Key insight: Ancient treaties included: - Divine witnesses from both pantheons - Curse formulas invoking these gods - Often tribute including temple vessels - Sometimes placing vassal deities in overlord's temples - Installation of overlord's cult in vassal territory </notes>\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl280\sa240\partightenfactor0
