Opus:\
The judgment's precise reversal pattern, if predicted in advance, becomes undeniable when experienced. When Jerusalem's paid allies strip her naked (v.39), taking back the very gifts she gave them, the exiles experience their theological inversions physically. The Egyptian "protection" they purchased becomes Egyptian participation in plunder. This isn't generic conquest but their specific choices becoming their specific punishment.\
The "many women watching" (v.41) creates a particular recognition. Other nations Jerusalem tried to impress by her alliances now witness her shame. The exiles in Babylon, living among these watching nations, cannot maintain the fiction that this was private political miscalculation. The international witness makes the judgment's meaning public and undeniable.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl280\partightenfactor0
\cf2 <notes> The restoration promise in vv.60-63 only makes sense if judgment first establishes YHWH's justice Without accepted guilt, restoration looks like fickleness With accepted guilt, restoration demonstrates undeserved grace </notes>\
\pard\pardeftab720\sl280\sa240\partightenfactor0
