\f0 \cf2 " (I will be calm and no longer angry) - creates a theological crisis that produces recognition. If YHWH's anger is satisfied by exactly what happened to Jerusalem, then either the punishment perfectly fit the crime (proving both power and justice), or YHWH is claiming credit for coincidence (unsustainable when the details match too precisely).\
The oracle given in advance functions like a sealed indictment. When events unfold exactly as described - not just defeat but this specific form of defeat by these specific nations with these specific humiliations - the advance notice prevents claiming randomness. The exiles must explain how Ezekiel knew Babylon would strip Jerusalem's wealth, burn her houses, expose her to international shame, and then stop.\
The child sacrifice detail (vv.20-21) gains particular force after judgment. When Jerusalem's children are actually slaughtered by Babylonians, the parallel to sacrificing children to Molech becomes unbearable. They killed YHWH's children for foreign gods; now foreign armies kill their children. The symmetry is too precise for coincidence.\
This produces recognition not through argument but through experience. Living through exactly what was described, in the precise form predicted, with the specific nations involved, creates knowledge that rhetoric couldn't. They "know that I am YHWH" because only YHWH could orchestrate their own choices becoming their judgment with such precision.\
